            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for to succeed, then the Russian for to work out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: гарантировать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гарантировать (garantírovat) — \"to guarantee\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Я не могу гарантировать, что всё получится. Ya ne mogú garantírovat, chto vsyo polúchitsya. I cannot guarantee that everything will work out."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The same form serves as both imperfective and perfective; present гарантирую, гарантируешь."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гарантировать (garantírovat) is usually traced, through German, to French garantir \"to guarantee\" (EtymDB), built on garant \"a guarantor\"; EtymDB sets garant beside Old High German werento \"a guarantor\" (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
